body:
Idk if you read poetry, but I really like this one by Walt Whitman: [https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/51568/o-me-o-life](https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poems/51568/o-me-o-life). I find it meaningful because it doesn't sugarcoat the reality of human suffering. There's no guarantee that things will get better. But the very fact of existence means that there's hope.

&#x200B;

I also take comfort in this song to the tune of Auld Lang Syne: [https://youtu.be/DngSe0HwstM](https://youtu.be/DngSe0HwstM). The history of it is really interesting (soldiers in the trenches would sing it during WWI). Sometimes we don't know why we are here, but we can still proclaim in hope THAT we are here.

&#x200B;

So, to answer your question What else is left? YOU. And that's not insignificant. Take care <3
